rName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"b4b76423feb220db7e78f27e769f3d32ffaf89b7","date":"2026-09-28T16:06:21+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5916: Reuse generated identifiers when retrying a patient save (#2780)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"81c24905675b9e4228681e1d1465497226f8d2d7","date":"2026-09-25T21:10:51+03:00","message":"(BREAKING) Remove offline support from patient management (#2776)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"ddd67a6674f8dd70f26bd01b36b2ce5d5098e67f","date":"2026-08-24T22:27:05+03:00","message":"(fix) O3-5913: Wait for patient data deletions before reporting save success (#2697)","refs":"","body":"* fix: await patient data deletions\n\nWait for name, identifier, and attribute deletions before saving the patient. Propagate deletion failures so the UI cannot report a successful update when cleanup fails. Add regression tests for pending and failed deletion requests.\n\n* test: strengthen identifier deletion coverage\n\nFlush the event loop before checking that the patient save is still pending. This makes the regression test fail against the previous unawaited identifier deletion path.\n\n* chore: remove unused attribute parameters\n\nSimplify the patient attribute payload builder now that deletion handling runs in the asynchronous save stage.\n\n* fix: wait for concurrent requests to settle\n\nWait for every patient-data request to finish before propagating a failure. Add mixed pending-and-failure tests for name, attribute, and identifier operations.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"},{"hash":"f298c04173e456f92b94fcd90d781c8b89d0e157","date":"2026-08-24T16:45:51+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5919: Clear stale death metadata when marking a patient alive (#2694)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Kavitha Kanchana","authorEmail":"146015143+kanchana404@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"b62a38834ec4351e7292b9d4d19229eee715e24c","date":"2026-08-24T15:57:44+05:30","message":"(fix) O3-5910: Preserve local-language names when editing a patient (#2693)","refs":"","body":"","authorName":"Kavitha Kanchana","authorEmail":"146015143+kanchana404@users.noreply.github.com"},{"hash":"5fc0dc3f780ec9c00c40e48e3215b805eca2bc26","date":"2026-05-13T20:23:11+03:00","message":"(chore) Migrate from jest to vitest (#2532)","refs":"","body":"* (chore) Migrate from jest to vitest\n\nSwap the test runner from jest to vitest across all nine workspace\npackages, aligning patient-management with the patterns adopted\nacross the rest of the O3 apps.\n\n- Root: replace jest, @swc/jest, jest-cli, jest-environment-jsdom,\n  and @types/jest with vitest, @vitest/coverage-v8, jsdom, and\n  bumped cross-env (7.x to 10.x). Bump @testing-library/dom (9 to 10),\n  @testing-library/jest-dom (6.1 to 6.8), and @testing-library/react\n  (14 to 16) so the /vitest subpath is available. Delete the root\n  jest.config.js.\n- Add a single root vitest.config.ts shared by all packages. Uses\n  jsdom; aliases .scss/.css to identity-obj-proxy via the anchored\n  ^.*\\.s?css$ regex; uses exact-match regex aliases (e.g.\n  /^@openmrs\\/esm-framework$/) for @openmrs/esm-framework and\n  @openmrs/esm-translations so the alias does not capture the\n  /mock subpath; aliases react-i18next to the local __mocks__ file;\n  exposes the tools and __mocks__ paths the way the jest config did\n  via moduleDirectories; pins uuid to the top-level install so\n  esm-offline's nested uuid wrapper doesn't blow up under ESM; caps\n  fakeTimers.toFake so it does not break React's scheduler. Sets\n  process.env.TZ = 'UTC' so the test scripts can drop cross-env.\n- Update tools/setup-tests.ts to load @testing-library/jest-dom/vitest\n  and swap jest.* for vi.* across the mocks (single-spa,\n  scrollIntoView, matchMedia, ResizeObserver-as-class).\n- Update every package's test scripts to `yarn run -T vitest run\n  --passWithNoTests` etc. The -T flag tells yarn 4 to resolve the\n  binary from the top-level workspace.\n- Convert the 100+ test files to the vitest API: jest.* swapped for\n  vi.*, jest.Mock and jest.SpyInstance type aliases replaced with\n  Mock and MockInstance from vitest. The many vi.mock(path, () =>\n  ({ ...jest.requireActual(path), override })) factories rewritten\n  as the async vi.mock(path, async () => ({ ...((await\n  vi.importActual(path)) as object), override })) form; the `as\n  object` cast keeps eslint's consistent-type-imports rule happy\n  without per-module type imports. Several vi.mock(name, () =>\n  vi.fn()) factories wrapped in { default: vi.fn() } so the\n  factory returns a module object. vi.mock('@openmrs/esm-framework',\n  () => ({ X })) calls in useWardLocation.test.ts and\n  side-menu.test.tsx rewritten as the importOriginal-spreading form\n  so the partial override does not lose the rest of the framework\n  exports.\n- patient-management/packages/esm-ward-app/mock.tsx: this is loaded\n  as a test fixture by ward-view tests, so its inline jest.mock and\n  jest.fn calls are swapped for vi.mock and vi.fn and a top-level\n  `import { vi } from 'vitest'` is added.\n- Replace two `jest.replaceProperty` usages (in ward-view and\n  admit-patient-form tests) with a small local replaceProperty\n  helper, since vitest has no direct equivalent.\n- Rewrite the IntersectionObserver mock in ward-view.test.tsx and\n  the ResizeObserver mock in tools/setup-tests.ts as ES classes;\n  vitest's vi.fn().mockImplementation(...) is not constructable.\n- Add explicit `import { vi, describe, it, expect, ... } from\n  'vitest'` to test files. Where the field.resource mock uses jest.fn\n  outside a test file, also import vi.\n- Rewrite the xit in appointments/appointment-tabs.test.tsx as\n  it.skip; xit is not a vitest global.\n- Skip one pre-existing field.test.tsx case\n  (`should render AddressComponent component when name prop is\n  \"address\"`) that performs vi.mock inside an it() and relied on\n  the implicit jest.fn return; it never set a return value via\n  mockReturnValue so the component crashed. Flagged with TODO for a\n  follow-up.\n\n692 tests pass across 8 packages (2 skipped). All packages green\nunder tsc; eslint clean.\n\n* (chore) Address PR review: drop jest shims, fix watch script, add coverage thresholds\n\n- Delete the nine per-package jest.config.js files that re-exported\n  the root config. The root config was already deleted by the\n  migration, so these were broken entry points.\n- Update packages/esm-appointments-app's test-watch script (it still\n  pointed at jest --watch --config jest.config.js) to use vitest watch.\n  Other packages were already updated; this one slipped through\n  because its key was test-watch rather than test:watch and didn't\n  match the original migration's perl rewrite. Renamed to test:watch\n  for consistency.\n- Port coverage configuration from the deleted jest config to\n  vitest.config.ts: 80% global threshold and the same\n  collectCoverageFrom restriction to **/src/**/*.component.tsx.\n\n* (chore) Use fileURLToPath and document the field.test.tsx skip\n\nTwo follow-ups from review:\n\n- vitest.config.ts relied on new URL(...).pathname for setupFiles and\n  six aliases. On Windows .pathname yields /C:/... which is not a\n  valid filesystem path. Add a fileURLToPath helper and route every\n  URL-based path through it, matching the pattern adopted in\n  openmrs-esm-form-builder.\n- The PR body says the field.test.tsx it.skip is flagged with TODO,\n  but no comment was added. Add one explaining why the test is off.\n\n* (chore) Drop dead @openmrs/esm-framework/src/internal alias\n\nvitest.config.ts aliased @openmrs/esm-framework/src/internal to\n@openmrs/esm-framework/mock, but no test file in the repo imports\n/src/internal — the alias was copy-pasted from a sibling project\nand never resolved any module here. Remove it.\n\n* (chore) Hoist replaceProperty helper into tools/\n\nward-view.test.tsx and admit-patient-form.test.tsx each carried a\nbit-identical 8-line replaceProperty helper — the local fill-in for\njest.replaceProperty, which vitest does not implement directly.\n\nMove the helper into tools/test-utils.tsx and export it from tools/,\nalongside the other shared test utilities. Both call sites now import\nit from 'tools' like they do for renderWithSwr.\n\nThe helper's behavior is unchanged: it swaps a writable own property\nand returns a {restore()} handle. The body adds a comment noting it\ndoes not handle getter or non-writable descriptors, which jest's\nreplaceProperty does — neither caller relies on that path.\n\n* (chore) Make each app have independently runnable vitest tests\n\nMirrors the pattern Ian introduced for openmrs-esm-patient-chart in\nPR #3301: a single shared vitest config in tools/, a thin re-export at\nthe workspace root, and a thin merge shim per app. With this in place,\n'cd packages/<app> && yarn test' works without bouncing through the\nworkspace root.\n\n- tools/vitest.shared.ts: the actual config that used to live at\n  vitest.config.ts, with the alias and setupFiles paths rebased from\n  './tools/...' and './__mocks__/...' to './...' and '../__mocks__/...'\n  respectively (it now lives one directory deeper).\n- vitest.config.ts: collapsed to 're-export the shared config' so\n  running 'vitest' at the repo root keeps working.\n- packages/*/vitest.config.ts: nine new thin shims, one per app, that\n  do mergeConfig(sharedConfig, {}). Each app now has a discoverable\n  config when vitest is run from inside the app directory.\n- packages/*/package.json: drop the '-T' flag from the test scripts\n  ('yarn run -T vitest run --passWithNoTests' -> 'vitest run\n  --passWithNoTests'); add 'vitest' as a per-app devDependency so the\n  binary resolves under yarn 4 without the workspace-root hop.\n\n692 tests pass across the 8 packages that have tests (esm-home-app has\nnone); 2 skips unchanged.","authorName":"Dennis Kigen","authorEmail":"kigen.work@gmail.com"}],"totalCount":8}"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"23eb3d2c-b7b8-4b24-b715-52d9abf335b7","uuid":"2a542d59-77fd-4975-a016-74fb9235e278","timestamp":"2026-10-23T15:01:26.379Z","tool_use_result":[{"type":"text","text":"{"commits":[{"hash":"1aaae8c003d0ce38c32f07617277398079ccb66a","date":"2026-10-05T08:48:57-04:00","message":"(feat) O3-1830: Allow selecting the preferred patient identifier during registration (#2786)","refs":"","body":"* (feat) O3-1830: Allow selecting the preferred patient identifier during registration\n\n* O3-1830: Deleting the preferred identifier row promotes a fallback\n\n* O3-1830: Guard the preferred option in the Edit mode\n\n* Update packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.ts\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\n\n* Update packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/input/custom-input/identifier/identifier-input.component.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\n\n* O3-1830: apply the suggestions for the screen reader\n\n* Update packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/form-manager.test.ts\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\n\n* O3-1830: address request ordering comments\n\n* Update packages/esm-patient-registration-app/src/patient-registration/input/custom-input/identifier/identifier-input.component.tsx\n\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n* O3-1830: align preferred radio buttons\n\n* O3-1830: The Identifiers section now uses full width when that preferred option is on\n\n* O3-1830: skip the client-side promotion when the user doesn't have the edit privilege\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Dennis Kigen <kigen.work@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Ian <52504170+ibacher@users.noreply.github.com>","authorName":"Cosmin","authorEmail":"cioan@pih.org"},{"hash":"b322ea70dcbc8614774d7b363ca1abca07fe07f0","date":"2026-09